things with this ordinance is it only applies to structures that are contributing within a historic district so it would not would not apply to a home that is not deemed as contributing what is a contributing structure a contributing structure within a district is one that exemplifies some type of architectural significance whether it's building style building period historic events that contributes to the overall character of the historic district um for example a lot of folks are very familiar with the Craftsman type of building style you have Victorian building styles those can be contributing I'm provided that they are maintaining some of their original materials and they haven't had additions that might render it non-contributing um I can use an example that we have in the community of a building that is believed to be contributing but is not contributing due to additions the aims help house is one that everyone's familiar with the additions on the back the addition of the metal and

